From a9f66e9eaae41f25c42ae4f502c3f57fbf52e290 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cheol Ho Choi <cheolho.choi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 22:12:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat: MRSF gradient through the Route-C bridge (G-5)

Two additions on top of the APIV2 response bridge:

1. int2_routec: dispatch the int2_tdgrd_data_t consumer (MRSF/SF/TD
   Z-vector iteration + relaxed-density builds). Verified table (G-5
   phase A(i), numpy Z-vector port vs native relaxed densities, td_p/WAO
   rebuilt to ~2e-8, wrong-prefactor controls fail at 1e-2..1e0):
     apb_s = c*J(Ms_1 + Ms_2) - x*K(Ms_s),  Ms_s = d2_s + d2_s^T
   (Coulomb of the spin-summed symmetrized density in BOTH slots,
   exchange spin-diagonal); amb slot 1 only, as TD RPA. One-time stderr
   notices record which consumers were diverted in a run.

2. routec_bridge + tdhf_mrsf_gradient: optional external supplier for the
   MRSF 2e ERI-derivative contraction. $OQP_ROUTEC_GRAD_LIB ->
   routec_grad2_mrsf(d, p, spc, xyz, de, nbf, natm, hfscale, hfscale2,
   coulscale, spcscale, mrst, info) bind(C); mrsf_2e_grad passes the RAW
   alpha/beta SCF + relaxed densities and the 7 MRSF response densities
   (before the grd2 init() sum/diff transform), no CAM, rank-0 compute
   with broadcast, info/=0 falls back to the native grd2 path unchanged.

Gates (H2O/6-31G* MRSF mult-3 ROHF, target S1; libintRot
test/routec_oqp_grad.cpp + sessions/20260612_grad_g5):
 - exact-Cholesky-B full-bridge run reproduces native relaxed densities
   (td_p 6e-10, WAO 3e-11) and the S1 gradient to 3e-11;
 - injected DF 2e gradient: end-to-end kernel consistency 1.6e-10;
   injected-vs-native = DF physics 4.8e-6 (HF) / 6.4e-6 (BHHLYP) Ha/bohr;
 - FD referee (Richardson): native analytic vs FD 3.9e-9 (HF); the
   BHHLYP 5.5e-5 residual is XC grid quadrature (1.1e-6 on a 99,590
   unpruned grid), identical for native and injected;
 - CH2O S1 optimization demo: native and injected reach the same minimum
   to 4.8e-5 bohr (interatomic distances), dE = -2.9e-9 Ha.

